01:33:37.148 --> 01:33:40.652
says maintain a 2-foot Radius free from artificial

01:33:40.684 --> 01:33:44.070
turf? Yeah, it's only the— it's the composition

01:33:44.570 --> 01:33:48.804
of the sentence. Tree trunks maintain— tree trunks shall maintain, and it's like,

01:33:48.869 --> 01:33:52.367
you're going to enforce it with a tree? The subject should be the space.

01:33:52.961 --> 01:33:56.604
I gotcha. Minor, like it's more like a direction.

01:33:56.684 --> 01:33:59.878
A tree ring that's 2 feet, 2.5 feet. Anyway, okay.

01:34:00.761 --> 01:34:04.340
Steven? I just— I wanted to point out that

01:34:04.587 --> 01:34:08.044
You've been talking about this 50% requirement. Right before that in

01:34:08.060 --> 01:34:11.759
the code, it does mention that that requirement only applies to

01:34:11.791 --> 01:34:15.491
building permits. So properties that have building permits that are issued after February 1st,

01:34:15.507 --> 01:34:19.223
2024. Right. So that'd be all your

01:34:19.723 --> 01:34:24.004
newer builds. And it's kind of— maybe this question for Marcus too. So what— could

01:34:24.020 --> 01:34:27.668
this ever apply if a property completely

01:34:27.684 --> 01:34:30.479
changes their landscaping? So, or does it really just tie to their building permit?

01:34:32.384 --> 01:34:36.118
I would say that if they were changing their landscaping and

01:34:36.230 --> 01:34:39.355
putting in artificial turf, it would absolutely apply. Okay.

01:34:39.980 --> 01:34:43.104
Would it be better to change this wording though to make that a little clearer?

01:34:44.226 --> 01:34:47.607
To clarify that it applies to

01:34:47.767 --> 01:34:50.459
anybody putting in artificial turf? I think— Well, just to— I mean,

01:34:51.132 --> 01:34:54.946
I've had this question. I think just it being there, those are just the standards

01:34:55.042 --> 01:34:58.594
for artificial turf that we have. Had already legally put

01:34:59.094 --> 01:35:02.839
in artificial turf, then you would you could be nonconforming theoretically.

01:35:03.016 --> 01:35:06.406
But if you have like grass and you know

01:35:06.906 --> 01:35:10.462
other vegetation in your yard and you want to put in artificial turf to replace

01:35:10.962 --> 01:35:14.015
a large portion of that up fifty seventy five percent whatever the number is,

01:35:15.567 --> 01:35:18.528
then you'd have to follow these standards because that would be the standard that applies

01:35:18.576 --> 01:35:21.891
in our code at the time you're doing the act. So I don't know that

01:35:21.923 --> 01:35:25.501
you need to. Put it in clarifying that

01:35:26.001 --> 01:35:29.488
it applies to existing homes any more than you would have to put it

01:35:29.988 --> 01:35:33.928
in any other code requirement that it applies to an

01:35:34.428 --> 01:35:37.917
existing home that wants to engage in a use that they're not conforming on.

01:35:43.480 --> 01:35:46.751
Okay. Good discussion. Okay.

01:35:47.723 --> 01:35:48.355
Any other comments?

01:35:52.828 --> 01:35:56.241
I'll just say I'm glad we're writing this because this is really good to have

01:35:56.741 --> 01:35:58.898
because I've seen it come on the news before with other cities doing it and

01:35:59.010 --> 01:36:02.681
having problems with the runoff and all that other kind of stuff when people bring

01:36:02.713 --> 01:36:06.420
turf in. And so having some standards is really, I think, is smart

01:36:06.920 --> 01:36:10.030
and helpful. So grateful for it. Yeah.

01:36:11.643 --> 01:36:15.115
Well, the city does have one area of artificial turf

01:36:15.615 --> 01:36:16.149
out there, Eagle Mountain Boulevard.

01:36:18.957 --> 01:36:22.326
And high school. Well, yeah,

01:36:22.390 --> 01:36:27.165
yeah, yeah. Be careful what you wish for, I guess,

01:36:27.278 --> 01:36:31.984
because it's hot stuff. It's not cool

01:36:32.760 --> 01:36:34.215
by any stretch. But anyway,

01:36:36.138 --> 01:36:39.354
yeah, okay, I will entertain

01:36:39.612 --> 01:36:43.670
a motion for this agenda. Item 7C.

01:36:54.798 --> 01:36:58.267
Do you want to try? Yeah. OK.

01:36:58.574 --> 01:37:02.849
I think the only suggestion we really came to was just some language

01:37:02.866 --> 01:37:07.215
consideration for, right, item E

01:37:07.279 --> 01:37:10.306
to make the emphasis on the space,

01:37:11.460 --> 01:37:15.002
the free, the 2.5-foot tree ring. We usually call those tree

01:37:15.502 --> 01:37:18.367
rings free from artificial turf. That would be the only thing, I think, other than

01:37:18.867 --> 01:37:22.774
that. But you're welcome to make that. Okay, I move that

01:37:23.274 --> 01:37:27.004
we— I believe the action is to forward a positive recommendation to City Council for

01:37:27.181 --> 01:37:30.274
Item 7C with the change

01:37:30.450 --> 01:37:33.991
to Item E that we talked

01:37:34.040 --> 01:37:37.969
about probably something along the lines of artificial turf shall

01:37:38.469 --> 01:37:41.996
not be installed within 2.5 feet of the outer edge of the trunk of

01:37:42.496 --> 01:37:45.170
any existing tree measured at ground level. Something like that,

01:37:46.299 --> 01:37:47.084
or to that effect.

01:37:50.279 --> 01:37:53.926
Yeah. That's good. Okay. That make sense?

01:37:55.437 --> 01:37:59.149
I will second it. Okay. We have a motion

01:37:59.649 --> 01:38:03.909
by Commissioner DiCorsi. To forward a positive recommendation

01:38:04.409 --> 01:38:07.560
with a recommendation of language change, as well as a second

01:38:08.060 --> 01:38:11.987
by Commissioner Strong. Any need to clarify

01:38:12.197 --> 01:38:15.449
that? Okay. Any discussion?

01:38:17.148 --> 01:38:19.640
Okay. We'll proceed with our vote. We'll start with Commissioner Freeh.

01:38:20.820 --> 01:38:24.120
Yes. Commissioner Jensen. Yes. Commissioner DiCorsi.

01:38:24.394 --> 01:38:28.057
Yes. Commissioner Hess votes yes. And Commissioner Strong. Yes.

01:38:28.396 --> 01:38:32.277
OK, thank you. That vote passes with 5 votes.

01:38:34.162 --> 01:38:37.694
Moving on to our agenda. Thanks for the discussion, everybody. That was good.

